  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Open Contracting for Health (OC4H)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Government, Private sector, Civil Society</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public procurement in national health systems is made more transparent</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International Global Health Programme, with support from the UK&#x2019;s Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office (FCDO), concluded the Open Contracting for Health (OC4H) project in July 2021. The project, which ran from 2017 operated across Nepal, Kenya, Uganda, Zambia and South Africa, with TI&#x2019;s partner chapters implementing the in country work.

The project sought to improve health outcomes within the target countries by increasing the transparency of national health systems procurement systems.</narrative>
  </description>
